## Notes: Your own cooldown bars, built on Blizzard's Cooldown Manager. Pick the spells, arrange the grid, style each bar.
## Notes-deDE: Eigene Cooldown-Leisten auf Basis des Blizzard-Cooldown-Managers. Spells waehlen, Raster anordnen, jede Leiste einzeln gestalten.
## Author: Zwoelf - EU Destromath
## Version: 4.16.0
## SavedVariables: ZwoelfStuffDB
## AddonCompartmentFunc: ZwoelfStuff_OnAddonCompartmentClick
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\ZwoelfStuff\Media\logo
## X-License: MIT
## X-Category: Buffs & Debuffs

# Embedded libraries. Not a design decision reversed - LibSharedMedia is a
# REGISTRY, not a look: it is how the fonts and textures the user already has
# from their other addons show up in our pickers, under the names they know.
# Licences stay with the libraries: LibStub is public domain, CallbackHandler
# is BSD, LibSharedMedia is LGPL 2.1. Load order is dependency order.
Libs\LibStub\LibStub.lua
Libs\CallbackHandler-1.0\CallbackHandler-1.0.lua
Libs\LibSharedMedia-3.0\LibSharedMedia-3.0.lua

Core\Init.lua
Core\Media.lua
# The bar textures this addon ships, registered into the SHARED registry -
# so they sit next to everything the user's other addons put there, and are
# available to those addons in return.
Core\MediaLibrary.lua
Core\Secrets.lua
Core\CDM.lua
# The shipped proc database. Data, and it grows with every export, so it loads
# before the logic that reads it and stays a file you can paste into.
Core\KnownProcs.lua
Core\Auras.lua
# The arrangement engine, the visibility rules and the effects. All three are
# read by Bars.lua at file scope - BAR_DEFAULTS is built out of their default
# tables - so all three load above it.
Core\Layout.lua
Core\Visibility.lua
Core\Effects.lua
Core\Bars.lua
Core\Minimap.lua
# Widgets defines ns.UI, and EditMode reads it while it loads. Anything that
# takes a reference to the design system at file scope belongs BELOW this line.
Core\Widgets.lua
Core\Screen.lua
Core\EditMode.lua
Core\Changelog.lua
Core\OptionsBars.lua
Core\Options.lua
# Last, because it reads all of the above. /zs test - the checks that can only
# be run inside the game, which is every check this addon has.
Core\SelfTest.lua

# Deleted in 4.9.0: Core\Glow.lua, the expanding proc ring. It went with the
# single-aura window in 4.4.0 and nothing has called it since - it was still
# being loaded on every login for nothing. In the git history if wanted.
#
# Deleted in 4.4.0, and not coming back: Core\Display.lua and Core\Watcher.lua,
# the single-aura window and the aura hunt behind it. An aura is a cell on a
# bar now, so a second window showing one buff on its own was two answers to
# the same question. They are in the git history if anything is ever wanted
# back out of them.

# Parked until patch 12.1. Blizzard_AuraContainer does not exist before then,
# so every one of these is inert on a 12.0 client - verified in game, the
# engine probe fails outright. They are kept, not deleted, because the code
# is correct and 12.1 is days away.
#   Core\Engine.lua        the AuraContainer layer
#   Core\Catalog.lua       spell catalogue from talents and the spellbook
#   Core\Probe.lua         "does this spell ID bind?" diagnostic
#   Core\Groups.lua        engine-backed tracking groups
#   Core\CoTanks.lua       co-tank panel with engine aura strips
#   Core\OptionsGroups.lua the options page for the above
